#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Walks through the whole project on screen, captioned, for recording.

Everything shown is the real thing: the launcher's own artwork, the row built
from it, and the jukebox itself.  Only two things are stood in for - the audio,
because a virtual display has no sound card, and the launcher window, because
the real one needs Steam and Proton.

Meant to be recorded off a virtual display, so that it neither disturbs nor
depends on whatever is on the real one:

    Xvfb :90 -screen 0 1920x1080x24 &
    ffmpeg -f x11grab -draw_mouse 0 -framerate 30 -video_size 1920x1080 \
           -i :90 -t 62 -c:v ffv1 raw.mkv &
    DISPLAY=:90 tools/demo-tour

Then trim to the content and compress hard - screen recordings are mostly
still, so this costs almost nothing in sharpness:

    ffmpeg -ss 1.4 -t 59.4 -i raw.mkv -c:v libx264 -preset veryslow \
           -tune stillimage -crf 28 -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart \
           demo.mp4

Nothing it produces belongs in this repository: a film of the running
interface is a film of EA's artwork, which is why there are no screenshots
here either.
"""

import os
import sys

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
sys.path.insert(0, HERE)

